WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.440
Look how bright the children's
 eyes are shining.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.490
Here at Hatsuya Department, they're
 selling something children love.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.490
Bugs. That's right, insects.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.280
Kids would catch them in mountains,

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.740
but now, they're sold
 at department stores.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.790
Which bug do you like, young man?

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.620
What's that one up there?

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.710
Well, let me see.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.380
Could it be a big unicorn beetle?

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.210
That's today's main feature.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.630
It flew right into
 a jacklighting boat.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.050
Professors are saying
 it might be a new species.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.140
Wow, sounds interesting.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.720
It'll cost you at least 100,000 yen.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.480
4 months of salary?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.990
My 100,000 yen!

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.200
What can be happening?

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.450
A fog, a black fog.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:08.380
The Black Fog that's been disrupting
 transportation these few days.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.210
This must be it.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.680
What is this fog?

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.140
Don't worry.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.820
Thank you for saving me.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.650
What are they?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.370
They're Tartaros Bugmen.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.180
Go, report on it.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.430
You're a pro.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.180
But we couldn't
 use it for the show anyway.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.860
It's a ghost!

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.950
(August, the 41st of Shinka Era,
 Ginza)

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:39.590
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.520
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.730
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:54.520
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.740
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.610
Justice is not on my side

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.870
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.540
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.670
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.960
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:22.720
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.890
And they become the reason we live

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:33.480
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:38.530
Only those that keep searching

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.070
can become the future

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.410
Start the revolution!

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.880
(Inside the "Black Fog")

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.250
This place hasn't changed a bit.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.970
(Winner)

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.060
- Yay, I won!
 - Oh my.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.440
Then here's another one.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.940
This is a winner too.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.620
Nobody's here.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.040
Must be at college or working.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.680
(August, the 41st of Shinka Era,
 Harumi)

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.890
Meteortail.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.890
Hoshinoko. Witch powers...

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.360
Can only be used
 for helping humans, yes?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.570
But nobody's looking.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.240
We'll never be able to go back
 to our home like that.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.570
Oh, time for the news.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.370
You're doing it too, Ullr.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.370
As we have been reporting...

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.120
The Black Fog that appeared at 9 a.m.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.960
flowed from Ginza to Kasumigaseki.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.540
What can this be?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:20.960
No idea.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:25.630
There are so many superhumans
 and rivaling evils on this planet.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.800
Science, magic,
 different plant, future...

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.060
It could be any of those.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.140
Let's go. We've got work.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.100
Mr. Hitoyoshi! Why so suddenly?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.350
Besides, the key...

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.610
This is a superhuman shelter
 provided by the Bureau.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.860
I have a spare key.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.530
We have work. Get dressed.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.150
Is it the Black Fog?

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.120
No.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:57.210
But the Superhuman Bureau specializes
 in handling superhumans, yes?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:01.090
The government doesn't officially
 acknowledge superhumans.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.130
But they exist.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.840
Like me
 and aliens like Mr. Grosse Augen.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.510
To fight evil aliens
 and unknown beings.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.100
But they don't
 officially acknowledge it.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:17.140
In newspapers and TV,
 one photo would get you fired.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.810
Sometimes, humans get caught in
 the rivalry between superhumans.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.190
I don't like the word "rivalry."

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.110
Heroic superhumans are
 fighting evil forces.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.660
Our job is to handle affairs secretly,

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.660
and manage and protect superhumans.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.960
But isn't the Black Fog
 related to superhumans?

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.120
As far as we know,

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:44.590
there is no Black Fog in
 the superhumans we registered.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.050
Then what's our job today?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.470
First Security Division to
 the National Diet Building.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.310
Command the mobile unit
 as reinforcement.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.310
Guard Unit 1 and 2,
 check the survivors.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.520
Hey, Mr. Hitoyoshi.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.570
Mr. Jiro, where are you going?

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:07.570
Three, four.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.650
Here I go.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.780
Wait up!

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.500
No one could enter the Black Fog?

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.920
Why don't they use that
 robot detective for this?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.460
No way, because I'm a ghost.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.170
Always pulling pranks!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.220
Surround him with people.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.850
He can't pass through living things.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.190
Gosh.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.650
A ghost?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:49.740
Do it, Kikko.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.150
You called me that again.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.780
Meteortail.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.040
What are you doing?

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.500
Convenient body.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.500
You could travel as cargo.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.170
I'm no railroad package!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.830
Um, we're sorry.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.670
Health and Welfare Ministry
 sub-division.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.010
- I'm from Super Population Research.
 - Cute!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.970
Wow, that sounds so cool.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.680
The Superhuman Bureau, huh?

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.970
I've heard rumors of you guys.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.350
That there are people
 who protect superhumans.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.190
Huh? The Super Population
 Research Laboratory...

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.150
Superhuman... Where's the "Bureau"?

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.650
What is this thing?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.150
A ghost, I guess.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.160
Ogre Emi's kind, huh?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.570
Monsters and ghosts are different.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.080
Monsters are a different
 lineage from humans.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.330
It's a name for
 an old intelligent life form.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.080
- Ghosts are...
 - What?

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.290
We don't really know.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.380
They like to play with children
 and they never age.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.720
That's all we know.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.550
I've never seen a real one before.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.090
I see.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.600
So you're all superhumans too.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.930
I'm the only human here.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.140
Human?

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.770
Oh well.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.150
Sounds fun. Count me in.
 The Superhuman Bureau.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.360
Hey, now.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.360
We aren't recruiting right now.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.280
We just hired Kikko.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.620
I'll be blunt.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:24.250
We took you in to watch you
 so you don't make more trouble.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.710
We'll register you and
 regularly check your dwelling.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.670
I don't have a home.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.800
There was a kid
 I was friends with until recently.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.470
I got kicked out for too many pranks.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.760
So I'm a homeless ghost now.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.940
I bet you're surprised.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.900
Come on, let's go fight
 those Tartaros Bugmen.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.400
Tartaros? What's that?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.690
What? You don't know?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.860
The thing controlling the Black Fog.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:57.990
What did you say?

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:02.540
Boss, we can't contact the prime
 minister and others in the fog, yes?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.290
It seems so.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.620
But the Public Security Force
 is already on the move.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.670
Here you go.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.220
Hey, I'm not a real dog, you know.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:22.300
You might look like a child,
 but you're really not.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:23.680
Be good.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.850
I'll always be a kid,
 and I can always play.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.190
That's what a ghost is.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.360
You grow at a different speed
 from humans too.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.690
Humans all die after a few decades.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.740
But I'll still be a kid then.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.070
Aren't we perfect for each other?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.200
Hey, wait!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.250
What is it with girls, anyway?

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.180
There are no official statements,

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:06.680
but the prime minister
 and officials are inside...

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.480
I've heard of Tartaros Bugmen before.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.850
But it was ages ago.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.980
I believe they lived in
 a different world.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:20.110
If they're evil, there has to be
 a superhuman counterpart.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.450
Yes, those are the rules.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:26.290
But there are no signs of any so far.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.750
Come on, let's go home.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.330
Retreat!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.940
Superhumans of
 the Public Security Force.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.700
This really just might become our job.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.490
Ouch.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.200
It's the bug from this morning.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.040
I'm glad we met again.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.210
Again? When did we meet?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.670
I need a favor. I...

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.010
Sorry. There's someone I like.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.020
- I just met her...
 - That's not it.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.060
I just want to be friends.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:35.810
Friends?

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.110
- That's it?
 - Yes.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.610
It's my job as a ghost
 to be friends with kids.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.820
Sure thing.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.450
- My name is Campe.
 - I'm Fuurouta.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.870
Oops. I have to be going somewhere.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.120
See you later.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.960
Campe?

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:58.380
Was she a ghost too?

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.960
Hey, ghosts aren't supposed to
 play tricks on other ghosts.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.090
It says so in the ghost laws
 or something.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.760
So this is the place.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:11.260
(Hitoyoshi)

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.020
There are no official statements,
 but the prime minister...

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.310
Mr. Akita. Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:21.900
Not at all.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.610
Thanks for all you do, Professor.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.780
How's Jiro doing?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.030
He's a great help.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.450
So that is...?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.330
In South America before the war...

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:39.500
I was taken to a grave of huge insects
 that are said to be extinct now.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.250
The world was ruled by
 huge insects at first.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.970
Then amphibians, and then reptiles.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.260
But why did the huge insects
 concede their power?

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.680
Perhaps the Tartaros Bugmen

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:57.350
are their form after they
 moved somewhere and evolved.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.110
I have cultivated the virus
 I found at the grave.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:08.610
So this dragged them down from power
 3 hundred million years ago.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:09.780
Yes.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.950
Are they superhumans?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.740
No.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.200
They are invaders.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.750
Even if they're past rulers,
 there's no need to accept them.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.500
Welcome home,
 Young Master and Miss Emi.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.260
I'm sorry.
 We decided to eat out today.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.550
No worries.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.550
You've got work to do tomorrow.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.010
Yes sir.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.600
I know.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:41.650
So those two are living
 under the same roof.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:42.940
You knew?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.110
In college, Miss Emi was
 Prof. Hitoyoshi's assistant.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.150
That's how she met Hitoyoshi Senpai.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.990
And they got a job at the Bureau
 where the Professor is an advisor.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.740
But they live together.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.790
They're going out, so it's fine.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.250
I just wanted to let you know.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.830
I figured that out a long time ago.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.000
But it'd be weird
 to quit the Bureau now.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:08.970
You've got it wrong.
 I got a job to protect this planet.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.260
Wait, stop!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.340
I advise you to run , little boy.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:18.890
(August, the 48th of Shinka Era,
 Kawasaki)

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:22.980
I'm of the Superhuman Bureau.
 Don't get me wrong.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.400
I've looked everywhere for you.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.150
I've finally grown enough
 to fight you.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.530
What did you say?

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.400
Die, Fuurouta!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.580
Hitoyoshi!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.870
Long time no see, Fuurouta.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.290
You haven't changed a bit.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.500
Why are you here?

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.800
I've already told you, Campe.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:58.430
Campe?

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.490
(August, the 41st of Shinka Era,
 Superhuman Bureau)

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:21.000
The superhumans of the Public
 Security Force have all died.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:26.080
We can't let the Tartaros Bugmen
 run free any longer.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.710
Yesterday they said we're not needed.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.130
We can't overlook those that
 occupy the National Diet Building.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:33.590
I'll do it.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.760
- Way to go, Jiro.
 - But...

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.350
They might be superhumans
 that have turned to evil.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.520
So let me negotiate first.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.310
Beating bad guys, right?

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.350
Then I'll do it.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.690
- It's freezing.
 - Idiot!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.980
The virus is temporarily dead
 in liquid nitrogen.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.860
You're just here
 to meet with a lawyer.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.660
I know about them.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:00.450
I can easily enter the Black Fog.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.660
And I want to do something good too.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.080
Something good?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.920
If I succeed, let me join the Bureau.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.920
Fuurouta!

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.480
That's how you came.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.600
To where we were.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.900
We? What do you mean?

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.450
Why are you here?

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.990
Hey, it's you again.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.030
I'll save you.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.750
Take this!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.600
Did it work?

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.860
That was close.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.360
Hey!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:20.070
Don't get caught by humans
 or Tartaros anymore!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:21.820
You let it escape?

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:25.120
Nah, that one was just a big bug.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.290
I can talk with bugs and animals.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:33.290
I was the queen of Tartaros.

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:34.710
The queen?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.970
Still being young,
 I was captured by humans.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.050
I was about to be sold.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.600
But you saved me.

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.720
The Black Fog had come for me.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.390
Then you really are...

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:53.520
Since mythological times, Tartaros
 Bugmen had lived in Japan's woods.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.360
That was the contract with humans.
 However...

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:00.400
Today's politicians had
 forgotten the agreement.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.620
They sold off the national forests.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:08.040
The Tartaros Bugmen lost their habitat
 and came to punish the politicians.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.580
Together with the Black Fog.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.710
That means I...

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.840
So what happened to
 your people, Campe?

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:19.880
You know what it was that you threw.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:21.720
A virus...

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.680
Campe is the lone survivor
 of the Tartaros Bugmen.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.850
That's why you're here.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:33.560
I thought that you, at least,
 were my friend.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:34.860
I didn't know.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.690
I had no clue that
 you were the same as that bug.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.400
But still, I was happy.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.820
That there was still someone
 who would be friendly with us.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.570
But...

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.490
Stop.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:53.080
I told you.
 I had meant to attack you all too.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:56.130
Even if your goal was just,

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.510
your means was not of
 a superhuman of justice.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:00.710
It's fine.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:05.220
I've done something irreparable. So...

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:10.060
You think your single life is worth
 the millions you took from Campe?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.730
You could never compensate for it.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:20.150
But what difference would it make
 to take Fuurouta's life?

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:22.950
But I can't forgive him.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.490
Campe.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:28.120
You can't forgive him
 because you're friends.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.750
Because he's a friend,
 you can't forgive?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.000
Fuurouta. Look at me.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.510
I've grown up.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.840
But you're still the same as before.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.010
The way we are now,
 we cannot be friends.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.690
It was easier back then.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:57.770
Yeah.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:02.230
There were bad guys,
 and good superhumans beat them.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.900
I was a hero, too.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:06.360
Wasn't I?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.450
Since when did things
 get so complicated?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:14.000
No distinction between good and bad.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:17.120
You and I are enemies too. Why?

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:21.210
Is it because I'm forever a kid
 that I can't understand?

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:25.420
Then I want to grow up too.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.680
No, it's fine.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:29.720
You stay the way you are.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:32.520
It's fine.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.400
Now, to let Fuurouta join us or not.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.820
Those in favor raise your hand.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:45.950
I think he'll be useful.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.700
Having a ghost would be fun.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.910
Hoshino?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:56.790
I don't think this is a place
 for children to work.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:57.750
Besides...

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.630
I was against it from the start. So...

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.840
- Huh?
 - Why?

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:09.510
He thinks we fight evil
 and protect good superhumans.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:10.590
What?

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:15.140
If he's here,
 I'll always be able to remember that.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.190
So we need him.

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:21.810
It's fine.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:24.230
You stay the way you are.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:24:00.080
The one Metropolitan Police Department
 detective who handles superhuman cases

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.870
With the soul of justice
 in a steel body,

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.750
I work in secret for
 people's peace and safety.

00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:07.420
Don't call me superhuman.

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:10.340
I'm just a detective.
 Detective Raito Shiba!
